  "e5ee8a1abaef02a72898ae3fa7eac281cd13422f55a5df5c9e4205b13136e5ed": "folyou - Jobs - Customer Success Manager Login Register Website Builder Features Responsive Website Examples Contact More Website ▾ Builder Features Responsive Website Examples Contact Site Manager Customer Success Work From Home Shifts - Online Support We are expanding our Customer Success team. If you are interested in internet marketing and setting up websites and want to integrate into a company where you will learn a lot and experience in a variety of areas of internet marketing - this is the job for you... Responsibilities: - Providing service and response to system customers by chat, email and phone. - Identify malfunctions, perform tests and report to developers. - Writing and editing explanations on the support website. - Website building and content management for websites. Job requirements: - Excellent written wording ability (perfect Hebrew and good English). - Great patience for humans. - Graduates of Internet marketing schools (advantageous). - Knowledge and experience in systems for building and managing websites (advantageous). - Knowledge of HTML (advantageous). To apply, send a CV to [email protected] . Good luck! Login / Register Special Opportunities for Folyou Clients Website Builder © Polio Folyou - Website Builder Contact Us Accessibility Statement Jobs What's New Support Terms of Use Privacy Statement Website for Business Promotional Sites FAQ Affiliate Program Affiliate Site Bilingual Virtual Store Register and start or register using Facebook Please enter your email address, and we will send your password to your email or login via Facebook ‹ Accessibility Search Close Search You are viewing the Accessibility Statement Accessibility Statement Accessibility Statement We believe that everyone is welcome The rule is to enjoy visiting our site and therefore try to make the site clear and accessible and allow convenient browsing for assistive technologies. The site has been designed to meet the World Wide Web Consortium's AA-level accessibility guidelines. If you have encountered any accessibility problem on the site please contact us at [email protected] Navigation using a keyboard You can navigate and use the site using a keyboard only. To enable keyboard navigation, press the tab key. Pressing tab will take you to the next link (highlighted in yellow) and pressing shift + tab will take you back to the previous link. Pressing Enter will activate the different links. On forms where options can be checked - the option is selected using the arrow keys on the keyboard (up/down). In the media presentations on the website (photos/video), images can be exchanged using the arrow keys on the keyboard (right/left). Accessibility options menu * The accessibility menu is optimized for Explorer 10 or higher, Chrome and Opera browsers. On firefox andSafari browsers on Mac computers, enable keyboard navigation in the browser settings menu. Pressing the tab key will enable accessible site navigation. At the top of the site, you'll see the options: Accessibility Statement - Open the site's accessibility statement text. Skip to content - Start navigation from the main content area of the page (Skip navigation options in the top area). Skip to menu - Start navigation from the main site menu. Skip to search - Go to the search box on the site (if there is a search option on the site). Skip to the cart - Go to the shopping cart area (if there is a store on the site). Enable high contrast - change the color palette of the site to match color blind and visually impaired. Enlarge the caption on the site You can change the size of the texts on the site by using the Ctrl + keys or using the options menu in the browser (zoom). To enlarge the text on the site: Use the Ctrl + keys. To reduce the text on the website: use the Ctrl- keys. To reset the site text to its original size: Use Ctrl 0 keys. Text color and background color Clicking the \"Enable High Contrast\" button in the accessibility options menu eliminates the site's colors and background images. Texts will appear black on a white background. Content on the site includes standard labeling of headings, tables, paragraphs, lists, links, forms and buttons. Images on the site include an alternative description (Alt) if they are meaningful. The forms on the site are accessible to screen readers and keyboard users. The site may display content areas displayed from other sites as part of an iframe. Accessibility of these areas depends on the hosted site and we cannot guarantee their accessibility. For example - sharing buttons and a Facebook comment box, third party vendor clearing pages or any other plugin integrated into the content of the site. Additional accessibility aids The site is adapted for viewing mobile devices (responsive). The Aria site is used for orientation and use of the site using screen reader software. By signing up, I forgot my password. By submitting the form, you agree to the website's privacy policy. Cancel Forgot password By submitting the form you agree to the site's privacy policy. Personal details My bookings Disconnect from the editing system E-mail: Phone: Mailing confirmation: No Address: Gender: Other First and last name: E-mail: Phone: Password: Mailing confirmation: Yes No Address: Street: Number: Entrance: Floor: Apartment: City: Country: Select... Uganda Uzbekistan Öland Australia Ukraine Uruguay Azerbaijan United Arab Emirates Italy Bahamas Bouvet Islands South Georgia and South Sandwich Islands British Virgin Islands United States Christmas Islands Turks and Caicos Islands Minor Ottaling Northern Mariana Islands Marshall Islands Norfolk Islands Seychelles Faroe Islands Falkland Islands Pitcairn Islands Cocos Islands Cayman Islands Solomon Islands Indonesia Iceland Ireland El Salvador Albania Algeria Anguilla Angola Andor Islands Antigua and Barbo De Antarctica Estonia Afghanistan Ecuador Argentina Aruba Eritrea Armenia USA Ethiopia B